  "provenance": {
    "structure": "Region windows, roles and reading order were labelled by hand from 1.5x PDFium renders of all three pages. Reading order follows the visual flow: full-width items, then the left column top to bottom, then the right column top to bottom.",
    "geometry": "Region and figure bounds are measured (glyph-tight PDFium text bounds; union of vector paths). The table grid is measured from the vector ruling lines.",
    "text": "textStart/textEnd are PDFium's extraction (whitespace-normalised). Table cell text is binned into the measured grid and was checked against the render."
  },
  "repeatedElements": [],
  "uncertain": [
    {
      "id": "block-granularity",
      "what": "Paragraph granularity.",
      "why": "Blocks are visual blocks separated by vertical whitespace. Consecutive paragraphs set with only a first-line indent (no extra spacing) are one region: p0-abstract-body, p1-left-lead, p1-sec31-body and p1-sec34-body each hold two paragraphs."
    },
    {
      "id": "figure-before-caption",
      "what": "Figure precedes its caption in reading order.",
      "why": "Convention only. The PDF is untagged, so there is no structure tree to confirm it; the figure sits above its caption on both pages."
    },
    {
      "id": "continuations",
      "what": "p0-sec21-continued continues p0-sec21-body across the column break, p1-left-lead continues p0-sec3-body across the page break, and p1-right-lead continues p1-features-absent.",
      "why": "Judged by reading the text: each starts mid-sentence. The PDF encodes no link between them."
    },
    {
      "id": "footnote-position",
      "what": "p1-footnote-a is placed last (end of the right column).",
      "why": "It is a page footnote under a rule at the bottom of the right column; a reader could also meet it directly after the '4 Tables' text."
    },
    {
      "id": "authors-order",
      "what": "p0-author-1 before p0-author-2.",
      "why": "They are side-by-side centred blocks; left-to-right is the natural order but the PDF does not state it."
    },
    {
      "id": "table-position-in-flow",
      "what": "p2-table-1 is first on page 3, before '5 Conclusions'.",
      "why": "It is the table announced by '4 Tables' at the end of page 2; the split across the page break is inferred from the text."
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Text is heavily fragmented in PDFium: 228/381/121 text objects for pages 1-3, words split mid-word (e.g. '2 R' + 'elated Work', 'contemporar' + 'y ones'), and a '.' can be its own object. Anything working on raw objects must merge them (see groupIntoLines).",
    "Soft hyphens at line ends are extracted as U+0002 ('self-ref\\u0002'); joining hyphenated words across lines is not solved. Small-caps and spacing artefacts appear ('ANDWHITE', '1930’ s').",
    "The column gutter is only ~18pt (left column ends x=297, right starts x=315). Line grouping must use a horizontal gap below that (default max(14, 1.5 x height)); a larger gap merges justified lines across the columns.",
    "Page 2's keyboard figure is ~1049 vector paths plus ~117 single-glyph text objects (keycap labels). Those labels are part of the figure, not text regions.",
    "The page-3 table has a footnote row spanning both columns, so row/column counts depend on interpretation: 9 ruled rows x 2 columns with one merged cell (8 rows are header + 7 data rows).",
    "Hyperlink underlines are thin horizontal vector paths inside the table; they are not table rules and must be ignored when reading the grid (they are shorter than the table width).",
    "Reference entries use '[1]' and '[2]' markers; detectLists (A-3.2) does not recognise bracketed markers, so p2-refs-list is a reference list in the labels but not a detected list.",
    "No running header, footer or page number exists on any page (the template text on page 2 even says they should not be added), so none is expected."
  ]
}
